{"affected":[{"defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["tcp"],"original_ranges":[{"lessThan":"p5","status":"affected","version":"15.1-RELEASE","versionType":"release"}],"product":"FreeBSD","vendor":"FreeBSD"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-101307"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"datePublic":"2026-10-14T18:45:00.000Z","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"When the PCM sample array needs to grow, the RACK stack doubles a 16-bit allocation counter.  Repeated doublings caused the counter to wrap to zero, resulting in a near-zero-length allocation followed by a copy of the existing samples into the undersized buffer.  A remote peer can trigger the expansion by sending a sufficient number of ACKs on an established connection.\n\nA remote attacker who can establish a TCP connection to a system using the RACK stack can trigger an out-of-bounds write of approximately 512 KB in the kernel heap possibly resulting in a kernel panic."}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-122","description":"CWE-122: Heap-based Buffer Overflow","lang":"en","type":"CWE"},{"cweId":"CWE-787","description":"CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-15T07:05:02.295Z","orgId":"63664ac6-956c-4cba-a5d0-f46076e16109","shortName":"freebsd"},"role":"cna","title":"Remotely triggerable buffer overflow in tcp_rack"}],"assessment":{"authentication":null,"classifier_version":"1.0","confidence":"unknown","configuration":null,"entry_protocol":null,"product_class":null,"reasons":[],"relevance":"unknown"},"content_hash":"3fee72bb2f7ce8d0b9fae2ecc8d4f3367599fdf9e5acc63e842fc6bd195f6563","data_version":"5.2","first_seen_at":"2026-10-15T11:29:28Z","kind":"advisory","last_material_event_at":"2026-10-15T11:29:28Z","native_id":"CVE-2026-101307","provenance":[{"revision":"84c1500b89d4a5d9af483fd5109f4ddedbe1f5a7","source_id":"cve","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-101307"},{"assertion_index":0,"independent_evidence":true,"source_id":"cve"}],"published_at":"2026-10-15T07:05:02Z","record_encoding":{"expanded_bytes":3329,"expanded_sha256":"d09c7d6cbd02da5cb603269dbda51b1e13ab1b834e7558a4c0e1d71b47c0ca70","format":"cve-indexed-assertions-v1","top_descriptions_assertion_index":0,"top_descriptions_source":"descriptions"},"record_id":"cve/CVE-2026-101307","references":[{"assertion_role":"cna","provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-15T07:05:02.295Z","orgId":"63664ac6-956c-4cba-a5d0-f46076e16109","shortName":"freebsd"},"tags":["vendor-advisory"],"url":"https://security.freebsd.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-26:70.tcp.asc"}],"schema_version":"1.0","source_id":"cve","source_modified_at":"2026-10-15T07:05:02Z","status":"active","title":"Remotely triggerable buffer overflow in tcp_rack"}
